   "source": [
    "# Sparse Anatomical Memory\n",
    "## Interpreting BioMedCLIP representations for knee-imaging QA\n",
    "\n",
    "**Research question (main deliverable).** Given a *frozen* biomedical vision–language encoder, can a\n",
    "sparse autoencoder (SAE) learn latent features that are **more selectively associated** with anatomy,\n",
    "pathology, or imaging context than the original dense embedding dimensions?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Extension.** Can those sparse features be compressed into a **question-aware memory** that supports\n",
    "anatomical QA with far less information than the dense representation?\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements the full pipeline from the project outline:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Stage | What it does | Where |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| A | Frozen BioMedCLIP embedding extraction (cached to disk) | §2 |\n",
    "| B | Sparse autoencoder training (L1 or Top-K), dead-feature resampling | §3 |\n",
    "| C | Feature inspection: top-activating images per feature | §4 |\n",
    "| D | Text alignment against a controlled anatomical vocabulary + label selectivity **vs. controls** | §5 |\n",
    "| E | Question-aware sparse memory + QA compression trade-off curve | §6 |\n",
    "| Appendix | JEPA-style masked-region latent prediction (optional, off by default) | §8 |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Scope and honesty constraints (carried over from the outline).**\n",
    "* This is a **conceptual prototype**, not a clinically validated diagnostic system.\n",
    "* Features found here are **candidate** anatomical concepts until a qualified expert reviews them.\n",
    "* The notebook runs on a MacBook with `mps`, falls back to CPU, and **runs end-to-end with no data\n",
    "  download** by generating a controlled synthetic knee-MRI-like corpus with known ground truth.\n",
    "  If you point it at real knee MRI data (MRNet-style layout), it uses that instead.\n",
    "* Because the synthetic corpus has known generative factors (including *nuisance* factors such as\n",
    "  view, pulse-sequence contrast and scanner), it lets us test the outline's key warning directly:\n",
    "  **a sparse feature that correlates with a label may encode acquisition protocol rather than pathology.**\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "### Before you run\n",
    "Cell 1 sets configuration. Cell 2 checks/installs dependencies. Then `Run All`.\n",
    "Total runtime on an M-series MacBook: roughly 5–15 minutes on first run (model download +\n",
    "image rendering dominate), under a minute afterwards thanks to caching."
   ]
  },
  {
