   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-30",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 8. Appendix — JEPA-style masked-region prediction (optional)\n",
    "\n",
    "The outline is explicit that JEPA belongs in a *later* experiment, not the first training run. The\n",
    "cell below implements the minimal version of it: mask blocks of the image, re-encode the masked\n",
    "image with the same frozen encoder, and train a small predictor to recover the **embedding** of the\n",
    "intact image (prediction in representation space, not pixels). An SAE is then trained on the\n",
    "predicted representations and compared with the SAE from §3.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is an *approximation* of I-JEPA — real I-JEPA predicts target-block representations inside the\n",
    "ViT with an EMA target encoder, and trains the encoder itself. Here the encoder stays frozen, so\n",
    "this only tests whether representations reconstructed from partial views yield comparably\n",
    "interpretable features.\n",
    "\n",
    "Enable with `cfg.run_jepa_appendix = True` (adds one full encoding pass)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 34,
   "id": "cell-31",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "skipped - set cfg.run_jepa_appendix = True in cell [1] and re-run from here\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# %% [22] JEPA-style extension (off by default) -----------------------------\n",
    "if not cfg.run_jepa_appendix:\n",
    "    print(\"skipped - set cfg.run_jepa_appendix = True in cell [1] and re-run from here\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    MASK_PATH = os.path.join(cfg.cache_dir, f\"emb_masked_{ENCODER_KIND}_{sig}.npz\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    @torch.no_grad()\n",
    "    def encode_masked(paths, bs, block=64, n_blocks=4, seed=0):\n",
    "        rng_m = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n",
    "        out = []\n",
    "        for i in range(0, len(paths), bs):\n",
    "            ims = []\n",
    "            for p in paths[i:i + bs]:\n",
    "                a = np.array(Image.open(p).convert(\"L\"), np.float32)\n",
    "                for _ in range(n_blocks):\n",
    "                    y0 = int(rng_m.integers(0, max(1, a.shape[0] - block)))\n",
    "                    x0 = int(rng_m.integers(0, max(1, a.shape[1] - block)))\n",
    "                    a[y0:y0 + block, x0:x0 + block] = a.mean()\n",
    "                ims.append(preprocess(Image.fromarray(a.astype(np.uint8)).convert(\"RGB\")))\n",
    "            out.append(model.encode_image(torch.stack(ims).to(DEVICE)).float().cpu())\n",
    "        return torch.cat(out).numpy()\n",
    "\n",
    "    if os.path.exists(MASK_PATH):\n",
    "        Xm = np.load(MASK_PATH)[\"Xm\"]\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        t0 = time.time()\n",
    "        Xm = encode_masked(meta[\"path\"].tolist(), cfg.encode_batch, seed=cfg.seed)\n",
    "        np.savez_compressed(MASK_PATH, Xm=Xm)\n",
    "        print(f\"encoded masked views in {time.time()-t0:.1f}s\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    Xm_n = norm(Xm).astype(np.float32)\n",
    "    Ctr = torch.from_numpy(Xm_n[is_train]).to(DEVICE)\n",
    "    Cva = torch.from_numpy(Xm_n[~is_train]).to(DEVICE)\n",
    "\n",
    "    pred = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(D_IN, 1024), nn.GELU(), nn.Linear(1024, D_IN)).to(DEVICE)\n",
    "    po = torch.optim.Adam(pred.parameters(), lr=1e-3)\n",
    "    for ep in range(300):\n",
    "        idx = torch.randperm(Ctr.shape[0], device=DEVICE)[:cfg.batch_size]\n",
    "        loss = F.mse_loss(pred(Ctr[idx]), Xtr_t[idx])\n",
    "        po.zero_grad(); loss.backward(); po.step()\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        Ptr, Pva = pred(Ctr), pred(Cva)\n",
    "        cos_j = F.cosine_similarity(Pva, Xva_t, dim=-1).mean().item()\n",
    "    print(f\"JEPA-style predictor: cosine(predicted, true) on val = {cos_j:.3f} \"\n",
    "          f\"(masked-input baseline {F.cosine_similarity(Cva, Xva_t, dim=-1).mean().item():.3f})\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    seed_all(cfg.seed)\n",
    "    sae_j = SparseAutoencoder(D_IN, D_HID, cfg.sae_mode, cfg.topk).to(DEVICE)\n",
    "    oj = torch.optim.Adam(sae_j.parameters(), lr=cfg.lr)\n",
    "    Ptr_np = Ptr.detach().cpu().numpy()\n",
    "    for ep in range(cfg.epochs):\n",
    "        perm = torch.randperm(Ptr.shape[0], device=DEVICE)\n",
    "        for b in range(max(1, Ptr.shape[0] // cfg.batch_size)):\n",
    "            xb = Ptr.detach()[perm[b * cfg.batch_size:(b + 1) * cfg.batch_size]]\n",
    "            xh, z = sae_j(xb)\n",
    "            l = ((xb - xh) ** 2).sum(-1).mean() + cfg.l1_coeff * z.abs().sum(-1).mean()\n",
    "            oj.zero_grad(); l.backward(); sae_j.project_decoder_grad(); oj.step()\n",
    "            sae_j.normalise_decoder()\n",
    "    sae_j.eval()\n",
    "    Zva_j = encode_all(sae_j, Pva.detach().cpu().numpy())\n",
    "    bp_j = np.nanmax(np.stack([lift_at_k(Zva_j, ATTRS[a], K_P) for a in ATTRS]), 0)\n",
    "    bp_0 = np.nanmax(np.stack([lift_at_k(Zva, ATTRS[a], K_P) for a in ATTRS]), 0)\n",
    "    print(f\"best per-unit lift   standard SAE {np.nanmax(bp_0):.2f} | JEPA-style SAE {np.nanmax(bp_j):.2f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"mean top-20 lift     standard SAE {np.sort(bp_0)[-20:].mean():.2f} | \"\n",
    "          f\"JEPA-style SAE {np.sort(bp_j)[-20:].mean():.2f}\")"
   ]
  },
